<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>

    <!-- NuGet Package Metadata -->
    <PackageId>Sendspin.SDK</PackageId>
    <Version>10.0.0</Version>
    <Authors>Sendspin Contributors</Authors>
    <Company>Sendspin</Company>
    <Product>Sendspin SDK</Product>
    <Description>Cross-platform SDK for the Sendspin synchronized multi-room audio protocol. Connect to Music Assistant servers and play synchronized audio across multiple devices.</Description>
    <PackageTags>sendspin;audio;multiroom;sync;music-assistant;streaming</PackageTags>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v10.0.0 - Encrypted Transport (BREAKING):
- The transport is now encrypted end to end (Noise KKpsk2). Plaintext is gone, and there
  is no downgrade negotiation: a 10.x client requires a server speaking the encrypted
  protocol (aiosendspin >= 7.0.0). Use the 9.x line for older servers.
- Clients now have a persistent Curve25519 identity. SendspinClientOptions.Identity is
  required; build it with SendspinIdentity.FromStore(store), NOT Generate(), or the client
  gets a new client_id every launch and silently loses every pairing on restart.
- Construction moved to SendspinClientService.CreateForDial(loggerFactory, options) with a
  SendspinClientOptions object.
- Pairing: Pairing PSK plus at most one optional pairing-code method, dynamic or static
  (CPace). Pairing configuration is
  local and manufacturer-defined: set it through ClientCapabilities; no server can change it.
- client/state reports 'available' as a boolean rather than the legacy state string.
- New source@v1 role for line-in/microphone capture.
- Neither connection teardown path waits for the peer's Close frame any longer: both now
  return as soon as ours is sent, so neither can block forever against a peer that never
  answers (#143 listen path, #160 dial path). This covers SendspinConnection.DisconnectAsync,
  which DisposeAsync calls with no cancellation, so an app exit could previously hang
  indefinitely. The socket is left in CloseSent rather than Closed until the peer replies or
  the connection is disposed.
- Undefined wire vocabulary removed: VisualizerTypes.Pitch and binary type 21 (the spec
  reserves 21-23), PlayerStatePayload.BufferLevel and .Error (the spec closes the player
  state object), and AudioChunk.Slot. Undefined player-audio types 5-7 are now dropped with
  a warning instead of being decoded into the audio pipeline, matching the C++ reference.
- See MIGRATION-10.0.0.md. The 9.x line remains maintained for now.

----

      Earlier release notes: https://github.com/Sendspin/sendspin-dotnet/releases
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2024-2026 Sendspin Contributors</Copyright>

    <!-- Enable source link for debugging -->
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

    <!-- Generate XML documentation -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- NativeAOT and trimming compatibility -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Sendspin.SDK.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Core dependencies -->
    <PackageReference Include="Concentus" Version="2.2.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Noise.NET" Version="1.0.0" />
    <!--
      Noise.NET is a managed wrapper over libsodium: every primitive on the mandatory
      transport (X25519, ChaCha20-Poly1305, AES-GCM, SHA-256) is a P/Invoke. It declares
      'libsodium >= 1.0.16', and NuGet resolves the lowest match, so without this line we
      restore the 2018 build - whose native binaries cover only linux-x64, osx-x64, win-x64
      and win-x86. Every ARM consumer then hits DllNotFoundException from inside the
      handshake. Referencing libsodium directly floats that floor: 1.0.22 adds linux-arm,
      linux-arm64, linux-musl-*, osx-arm64 and win-arm64 (plus eight years of upstream
      fixes). This is a deliberate pin, not an incidental one - dropping it silently
      reintroduces the gap, so it is covered by the linux-arm64 leg of the CI aot job. (#89)
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="libsodium" Version="1.0.22" />
    <PackageReference Include="Zeroconf" Version="3.7.16" />
    <PackageReference Include="Makaretu.Dns.Multicast" Version="0.27.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="8.0.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0" PrivateAssets="All" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />

    <!--
      The package carries vendored third-party source, whose licenses require their notices to
      travel with any distribution. Shipping the notices only in the git repository would not
      cover a consumer who only ever sees the .nupkg.
    -->
    <None Include="..\..\THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
